Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:23:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] CI: the scheduled stale-PWA alarm: stale-pwa.yml, its ci.yml
 step, the catalog flip (Part of #4369 and #4104)

PATCH BRANCH: sg-patch/ci-s2-stale-pwa-alarm-4369 (danswett/agent-bridge); the file is patches/ci-s2-stale-pwa-alarm-4369.patch.
APPLY ON: PR #4466's branch ci/stale-pwa-alarm-4369 (it needs quality/stale-pwa.ps1 from there): git apply patches/ci-s2-stale-pwa-alarm-4369.patch
FOR: Quality (workflow files).

.github/workflows/stale-pwa.yml runs every 4 hours and by hand: two read-only GETs (curl of https://app.slipgates.com/config.js, and the job's own read-only token listing the newest
commit on main that changed pwa/), then quality/stale-pwa.ps1 on what it read, so the run is RED when the served build is more than 24 h older than that commit or when either read fails
(a failed read leaves no file and the script fails closed). contents: read, no secrets, no write token, no continue-on-error. ci.yml's light job runs the script's tests; the catalog suite
flips to exists and names the job; the merge rule's exempt list names the workflow (a schedule on main that judges no pull request).

Tests: StalePwaWorkflowTests (schedule and dispatch only, read-only permissions, only two GETs and no secret, a failed read leaves no file, the script's failure cannot be swallowed) with
four breaks caught (a push trigger, a curl write, a swallowed failure, continue-on-error). actionlint and zizmor are clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
